## Beyond Code: GPU Snapshots & CUDA Checkpoint (2026-08-13)

After exhausting batching + I/O optimizations, the next frontier is **eliminating the
load-from-disk step entirely**. The key insight: our models never change between
restarts. Why deserialize them from EBS → CPU RAM → GPU every time?

### The Vision

```
Traditional:        Stop → Start → Import Python → Load models → Warmup → Ready (27s+)
With GPU snapshot:  Stop → Start → Restore snapshot → Ready (~2-5s)
```

Snapshot the entire process state (Python interpreter + loaded models in VRAM) after
initialization. On next start, restore the snapshot instead of replaying initialization.

### Available Technologies

#### 1. NVIDIA cuda-checkpoint (github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-checkpoint)

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| What it snapshots | GPU device memory (VRAM) copied to host RAM. CUDA objects (streams, contexts) released and recreated |
| CPU state | NOT handled — delegates to CRIU for full process state |
| Restore time | Not benchmarked publicly, but VRAM restore is memory-bandwidth limited (~5 GB/s) |
| Requirements | Linux, NVIDIA driver 570+ (basic), **580+ for container passthrough**, 610+ for IPC |
| Limitations | No UVM memory. No IPC shared memory. All in-flight GPU work must complete before checkpoint. Same GPU chip type required for restore |
| Container support | Driver 580+ adds container partial passthrough. Works with CRIU |
| Status | **Active development, not production-complete.** Feature set expanding per driver release |

#### 2. Modal GPU Memory Snapshots (modal.com/blog/gpu-mem-snapshots)

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| What it snapshots | Full CPU process (via gVisor) + GPU device memory + CUDA sessions/streams/contexts |
| Restore time | **2-5s** for workloads that normally take 20-45s cold start |
| Requirements | NVIDIA driver 570/575+, Modal's custom infrastructure (gVisor, not Docker) |
| Limitations | Alpha stage. Cross-host requires matching GPU hardware. No multi-GPU. |
| Container support | **gVisor only — NOT compatible with Docker or ECS** |
| Status | Alpha — `experimental_options={"enable_gpu_snapshot": True}` |

#### 3. Modal CPU-only Snapshots (modal.com/blog/mem-snapshots)

| Aspect | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| What it snapshots | Full container state (process tree, memory, FDs, CPU registers, filesystem) |
| What it EXCLUDES | GPU state, network connections |
| Restore time | ~1s for Python imports, ~3.5s for model load to CPU (still needs `.to(cuda)`) |
| Requirements | gVisor, CPU architecture match, driver version match |
| Container support | **gVisor only** |
| Status | Production on Modal with automatic fallback |

#### 4. CUDA Driver API (low-level building block)

```
cuCheckpointProcessLock → cuCheckpointProcessCheckpoint → [store VRAM to disk/RAM]
cuCheckpointProcessRestore → cuCheckpointProcessUnlock → [process resumes]
```

State machine: RUNNING → LOCKED → CHECKPOINTED → LOCKED → RUNNING.
Designed to pair with a CPU-side tool (CRIU). Same chip type required.

