#### Level 2: Full GPU Snapshot on S3 — Future (requires CUDA checkpoint maturity)

Goes further: snapshot the ENTIRE initialized state (Python + models in VRAM + avatar
loaded + warmup done). On restore, the process resumes mid-execution as if it never stopped.

**What it saves additionally over Level 1:**
- Eliminates Python import time (~3-4s after TF removal)
- Eliminates model deserialization (torch.load, .to(cuda))
- Eliminates warmup (CUDA kernels already compiled)
- Server ready in **~5-6s** (pure S3 download time)

**Snapshot size:** ~6-10 GB (VRAM state + CPU process memory)
**S3 download:** ~6-10s at 1000 MB/s

**When to pursue:** After NVIDIA driver 580+ is standard on AWS AMIs and cuda-checkpoint
+ CRIU integration is production-stable. Level 1 gets us 90% of the benefit today.

